From 8eaa8d41d7b02fea721ad7d673abb72a02704390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode): clamp scheduled decode verify rows to
 remaining max_tokens

Upstream-Base: 866fa1e1ef2ed2ee7bcdbb8deffaccccd5ecdd46

Rationale: When a speculative decode request approaches max_tokens under async scheduling or synchronous decode, scheduling 1 + num_spec_tokens verify rows allocates KV blocks and runs target attention/MLP rows for positions past max_tokens that check_stop immediately discards. Clamping scheduled decode new tokens and copy-placeholder widening to the remaining token budget (or remaining budget + 1 when sink rejection is active so the final committed output token still undergoes sink verification) eliminates wasted target verify rows without changing any cross-rank control flow.

Quality: Lossless; only verify rows beyond max_tokens (or beyond the sink-verified last output token) are omitted.

Tests: pytest tests/v1/core/test_copy_drafts_scheduler.py tests/v1/core/test_sink_draft_zero.py

Upstream-Status: Spark-DS41F local patch
---
 tests/v1/core/test_copy_drafts_scheduler.py | 97 +++++++++++++++++++++
 vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py             | 50 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 146 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

